The dead fall silent. A woman in a cloak of falcon feathers walks the length of the queue, and they turn to watch her like flowers after the sun.
"You're the new chooser. Skögul says you're careful." # speaker: freyja
"Half the slain are mine by right. Odin forgets that when it suits him. From today I name a whim each morning, and the worthy who match it come to Fólkvangr." # speaker: freyja
* ["Yes, lady."]
  "Good. I remember the ones who remember me." # speaker: freyja
  # fx: standing freyja +1
* ["I stamp by Odin's rules."]
  "Then Odin's rules now include me. Read the decree, little chooser." # speaker: freyja
  # fx: standing odin +1
  # fx: standing freyja -1
- She leaves behind a smell of apples and cold iron. Skögul lets out a breath.
"Two masters now," she says. "Don't get between them." # speaker: skogul
